# eliciter configuration. Copy to .env and adjust; .env is gitignored.
#
# Secrets are NOT duplicated here. The ArcadeDB password is read from indexia's own
# docker/.env at run time (see ELICITER_INDEXIA_ROOT), so there is exactly one copy
# of it on this machine and rotating it there is enough.

# ---- where the sources live -------------------------------------------------
ELICITER_INDEXIA_ROOT=/home/aphorikles/indexia
ELICITER_PERCEPTUA_POSTS=/home/aphorikles/perceptua/_posts
# Ad-hoc writing: .txt/.md files dropped in directly, plus markdown transcriptions the
# scan-misc skill makes from scanned handwritten pages. Defaults to misc/ at the repo root,
# which is gitignored — this is your material, not eliciter's, so it is not committed here.
ELICITER_MISC_DIR=/home/aphorikles/eliciter/misc
# Your tweets, one .md per tweet (scripts/import-tweets.sh fills it from an X archive).
# Defaults to tweets/ at the repo root, gitignored.
ELICITER_TWEETS_DIR=/home/aphorikles/eliciter/tweets
# Books you are reading outside arxiv, one .md per book (scripts/books.sh adds them).
# Defaults to books/ at the repo root, gitignored.
ELICITER_BOOKS_DIR=/home/aphorikles/eliciter/books
# audua's transcribed-session output: one YYMMDD_NNNN directory per recording, each with
# a summary.md. A session is material while it is recent (within audua.RECENT_DAYS, 30
# days) and drops out on its own after that — no status to set by hand; see
# eliciterlib/audua.py for why.
ELICITER_AUDUA_ROOT=/home/aphorikles/audua/processing/output

# ---- arxiv --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which categories are swept, and the interest and exclude terms, are not settings: they
# live in state/interests.json and are tuned with the tune-interests skill.
#
# How far back a weekly sweep looks, and the most papers one sweep pulls in total, across
# all categories (paged 100 per request, newest first, stopping at the lookback edge). A
# real week across the default five categories runs past 1000 — at 300 the sweep only
# samples the newest day or two. See README "Known limits".
ELICITER_ARXIV_LOOKBACK_DAYS=7
ELICITER_ARXIV_MAX_RESULTS=300
# arxiv asks for ~1 request per 3s. Do not lower this.
ELICITER_ARXIV_DELAY=3.0
# The reading queue holds at most this many papers. A sweep tops it up rather than
# replacing it: unread papers stay, read ones free a slot, rejected ones never return.
ELICITER_ARXIV_KEEP=3

# ---- local UI ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Binds 127.0.0.1 unless started with --tailscale (then this machine's Tailscale IP, over
# HTTPS). 8420 is indexia's UI; 8080 and 8765 are kept clear. scripts/ui.sh --port N
# overrides this for one run.
ELICITER_UI_PORT=8473
